{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090921-death-magic-for-healing-purposes","id":1090921,"title":"Death Magic For Healing Purposes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-10T16:45:20-07:00","id":1090921,"title":"Death Magic For Healing Purposes","content":"With creative thaumaturgy: can one make a spell that uses death magic as form of healing? I'm curious as I've been discussing with a player back and forth about it - I'd like some clarification if it is doable. <br /> <br /> The debate started with the questioning and usage of death armor but than transitioned into the discussion of using death as a form of healing with Death 5 - Deny The Reaper. How would it work - what level of Death would be needed?<br /> <br /> What spell would it need to be one that healed bashing, lethal, etc - Is this even doable?<br /> <br /> Curious on responses so I figured I'd get a discussion brewing :P .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T17:23:45-07:00","id":1090934,"title":"","content":"Death 3 Fraying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T00:44:33-07:00","id":1091004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090921-death-magic-for-healing-purposes#post1090921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With creative thaumaturgy: can one make a spell that uses death magic as form of healing? I'm curious as I've been discussing with a player back and forth about it - I'd like some clarification if it is doable.<br /> <br /> The debate started with the questioning and usage of death armor but than transitioned into the discussion of using death as a form of healing with Death 5 - Deny The Reaper. How would it work - what level of Death would be needed?<br /> <br /> What spell would it need to be one that healed bashing, lethal, etc - Is this even doable?<br /> <br /> Curious on responses so I figured I'd get a discussion brewing :P .</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say no, healing is already specifically the purview of Life. Deny the reaper isnt healing, its reversing decay and &quot;ending&quot; blindness, etc etc &quot;ending being a purview of death&quot;. Death Armor uses entropy to slow damage down enough that its no longer as lethal.<br /> <br /> I would allow death to slow down/stop stuff like bleeding, since &quot;ending&quot; is its purview and its ending bleeding,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T00:51:40-07:00","id":1091006,"title":"","content":"If it were to kill a tumor or virus, there could be a possibility. But again that's a very circuitous route. Death isn't precise surgery. It's about snuffing out (or depleting) what makes a living organism tick. Some say it's the soul. As an ST, I would allow it on the basis that it's an extended roll with penalties. Every roll also may cause damage to the subject with a Dramatic Failure causing outright death if not grave harm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T01:26:39-07:00","id":1091014,"title":"","content":"It was discussed <i>many</i> times before and it boils down to whether the mg allows it. One thing is certain for me, Arcana can either perfect or fray their respective Purviews and damage is a form of decay. Death Arcanum can and should at least address the issue somehow. Maybe don't make it lasting or make it costly, let it work differently by 'dissolving' the damage, degrading it from lethal to bashing and than even lower bashing to half of the amount. There is already a few Death spells in C.Thaum thread that try different approaches in regard of dealing or healing. Remember that most of the time you can craft a spell that does opposite. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1036568#post1036568\">Here</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1057080#post1057080\">here</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1005949#post1005949\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1026999#post1026999\">here</a>. Maybe there is more but you'll have to scavenge it on your own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T02:24:41-07:00","id":1091029,"title":"","content":"Arguments can be made to allow it.<br /> Arguments can be made against it.<br /> <br /> I allow it in my games. It comes down to table preference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><u><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Destroy Wounds</u></span></span></u><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice: Unraveling</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor: Potency</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Suggested Rote Skills: Empathy, Medicine, Survival</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Adepts of Death can attack the marks Death leaves on still-living Patterns, undoing damage from lethal wounds as its influence is unraveled. Each level of Potency heals two lethal damage. </span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wounds healed in this way don\u2019t leave scars, as the wounds are attacked on a direct metaphysical level instead of being traditionally \u2018healed\u2019.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach: The spell destroys aggravated damage. Cost: 1 Mana.</span></b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T02:56:08-07:00","id":1091034,"title":"","content":"Im surprised how many people ignore purviews.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T03:04:47-07:00","id":1091037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090921-death-magic-for-healing-purposes?p=1091034#post1091034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im surprised how many people ignore purviews.</div> </div> </div> </div>Super constructive input. Good contribution.<br /> <br /> I'm surprised how many people only look at purviews with a single, rigid definition in mind. Decay, absence, enervation, absence, and endings are all in the purview of death.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Unraveling decay can be interpreted as healing. (with decay as '<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">the process of declining in quality, power, or vigor')</span></span><br /> \u2022 Unraveling the ending (of one's life), the same. <br /> \u2022 Unraveling enervation (<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">a feeling of being drained of energy or vitality; fatigue) would necessarily have the opposite effect (giving them a feeling of being full of energy or vitality, and unfatigued).<br /> <br /> All of these are reasonable interpretations, they don't become less so because 'Healing' is under Life. <br /> You're allowed to do the same things with different Arcana. The book is pretty explicit about that, and if Purview meant that 'No other Arcana can touch this', that would be necessarily false.<br /> <br /> Note that just because these are <b>reasonable</b> interpretations, it doesn't mean that they have to be allowed at any given table. Hence most everyone in this thread saying it depends on your table.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T05:49:47-07:00","id":1091085,"title":"","content":"I already contributed, i cant argue with people who are saying they would allow it at their table.<br /> <br /> Using game mechanics i definitely would not allow players to remove health levels. I would probably let them downgrade health levels to at lowest bashing but they would have to heal that bashing properly. I would let them ignore would penalties.<br /> <br /> Unravelling is the practice of imparing or damaging things under an arcanas purview, it is not the practice of doing the opposite.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T05:54:05-07:00","id":1091086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090921-death-magic-for-healing-purposes?p=1091085#post1091085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unravelling is the practice of imparing or damaging things under an arcanas purview, it is not the practice of doing the opposite.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Read practices again. Unraveling damages phenomena under the arcanums purview, period. If you Pattern decay to spread you will damage the target. Unravel decay and you'll end up with target feeling better.<br /> Edit: Luckily whether you agree with it or not Death and Spirit can heal, just put them in respective state of Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 05-11-2017, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T06:03:33-07:00","id":1091087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090921-death-magic-for-healing-purposes?p=1091086#post1091086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Read practices again. Unraveling damages phenomena under the arcanums purview.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;&gt; <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Unraveling </b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">spells can significantly impair or damage phenomena under the Arcanum\u2019s purview, or directly inflict<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">severe damage using the forces of an Arcanum.</span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>That is what i said Death unraveling can impair or damage deaths purviews of &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Darkness, decay, ectoplasm, ghosts, the Underworld, souls, cold, absence, enervation, endings&quot;, it can not &quot;impair/damage &quot;healing&quot; because its not under the purview.<br /> <br /> Explain to me how damaging decay suddenly makes things better? It'd slow it down yes, or even stop it, but unravelling decay is not reversing it.</span></span><br /> <br /> Saying you can use other magic to overlap with stuff to get the same effect is fine, i think downgrading damage is tschnically &quot;healing&quot; but your actually just ending the healing process quicker than normal. With that sort of logic you can just use any of the arcanum to heal. I'll use fate to get really lucky my wounds suddenly close up quicker or make it so im destined to heal faster.<br /> <br /> (If somebody could speed up time fast enough that wounds closed instantly, then i would allow it, it'd be mechanically similar effect to healing but via a different arcana, so yes while others might allow death to remove health levels, i wouldnt go that far, they can get close but no removing actual health levels like &quot;knit&quot; spells etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 05-11-2017, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T06:08:02-07:00","id":1091088,"title":"","content":"Wound is manifestation of a decay. Unravel the wound and you'll end up with no wound. It's a moot point really. So lets just stop here. Also check the edit on my previous post(sorry).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T06:12:05-07:00","id":1091090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090921-death-magic-for-healing-purposes?p=1091087#post1091087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'll use fate to get really lucky my wounds suddenly close up quicker or make it so im destined to heal faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weell. This is another topic named &quot;why some people think Fate is broken&quot;. I think you could to some degree make it faster with Fate but nothing major.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T06:22:33-07:00","id":1091092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090921-death-magic-for-healing-purposes?p=1091088#post1091088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wound is manifestation of a decay. Unravel the wound and you'll end up with no wound. It's a moot point really. So lets just stop here. Also check the edit on my previous post(sorry).</div> </div> </div> </div>A wound is a manifestation of damage and the wound can decay/get worse, Unravelling the wound would stop it getting worse. Unmaking the wound <i>might</i> be able to get rid of it completely, ill give people that. But before mastery of death downgrading damage is all you'd get out of me. So yeh we can leave it there..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T06:50:55-07:00","id":1091102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090921-death-magic-for-healing-purposes?p=1091092#post1091092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A wound is a manifestation of damage and the wound can decay/get worse, Unravelling the wound would stop it getting worse. Unmaking the wound <i>might</i> be able to get rid of it completely, ill give people that. But before mastery of death downgrading damage is all you'd get out of me. So yeh we can leave it there..</div> </div> </div> </div>That's also a totally reasonable interpretation. And so we've come full circle.<br /> Whatever works at your table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T11:59:06-07:00","id":1091217,"title":"","content":"I'd rule you're not getting anything better than killing disease and the like until Mastery at which point I might take some Unmaking arguments. Most of the arguments I'm seeing fall squarely into archmastery territory as they mostly involve the targeting of a concept rather than a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T12:03:38-07:00","id":1091218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090921-death-magic-for-healing-purposes?p=1091217#post1091217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rule you're not getting anything better than killing disease and the like until Mastery at which point I might take some Unmaking arguments. Most of the arguments I'm seeing fall squarely into archmastery territory as they mostly involve the targeting of a concept rather than a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wound=thing that increases entropy in a biological system. It's not an abstract.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T12:32:52-07:00","id":1091228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090921-death-magic-for-healing-purposes?p=1091087#post1091087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Explain to me how damaging decay suddenly makes things better? It'd slow it down yes, or even stop it, but unravelling decay is not reversing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to consider things in a Greek perspective. Fundamentally, things exist as reflections of a platonic ideal. Each tree, for example, is a partial reflection of the fundamental supernal symbol of trees. Trees, as all things, are not collections of molecules, bound by the laws of conservation of matter and energy, but are indivisible reflections of their corresponding symbols. The only way for a tree to deviate from the fundamental symbol of tree, is through the incorporation of other symbols into its pattern. When you chop a tree into wood, you are not breaking it apart. Things are indivisible. Rather, you are creating a new symbol of wood, and introducing a Death pattern to the tree itself. If you were to remove this Death pattern, the tree would spring back, fully formed, all of its branches and roots intact again, because there would be nothing stopping it from reflecting the fundamental tree symbol once again.<br /> <br /> So in other words, all decay, both active and past, is a foreign influence on other symbols. It must fall under an arcanum, because all things fall under an arcanum, and the most fitting arcanum for it is Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 05-12-2017, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T13:00:31-07:00","id":1091236,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying that it has to be this way, but it would be kinda cool if Death healing was substantively different than Life healing. Like, if you are fraying/unraveling a wounds ability to contribute to your death, that might not mean that the wound seals up like it was never there; it could leave you with some pretty nasty scars.<br /> <br /> I'm sure you could approach healing with Death in a way that wouldn't have that side effect though. For example, in the 'Simple Question' thread, people are talking about going into twilight and then healing yourself while you are ephemeral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T13:11:34-07:00","id":1091244,"title":"","content":"You can also order an Ghost to possess you and then order him to spend their essence to heal the host, or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T13:43:46-07:00","id":1091257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090921-death-magic-for-healing-purposes?p=1091236#post1091236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm sure you could approach healing with Death in a way that wouldn't have that side effect though. For example, in the 'Simple Question' thread, people are talking about going into twilight and then healing yourself while you are ephemeral.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's sufficiently clever that I'd allow it. It makes use of actual properties of Death in an unambiguous way to achieve a desired result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T15:42:21-07:00","id":1091304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090921-death-magic-for-healing-purposes?p=1091236#post1091236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying that it has to be this way, but it would be kinda cool if Death healing was substantively different than Life healing. Like, if you are fraying/unraveling a wounds ability to contribute to your death, that might not mean that the wound seals up like it was never there; it could leave you with some pretty nasty scars.<br /> <br /> I'm sure you could approach healing with Death in a way that wouldn't have that side effect though. For example, in the 'Simple Question' thread, people are talking about going into twilight and then healing yourself while you are ephemeral.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the suggestion that Death Fraying be able to downgrade damage from lethal to bashing, and perhaps even cure some of the bashing, but not all of it. It's both accurate to the setting, and sufficiently different from Life healing to give Death its own distinction. Remember, Fraying can't utterly destroy a pattern - that would be unmaking. So it makes sense to me that a Death Fraying spell should be able to downgrade damage, but not eliminate it entirely. A Death unmaking spell, however, SHOULD be able to heal wounds completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 05-11-2017, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T18:28:31-07:00","id":1091365,"title":"","content":"Can't Death Unmaking straight-up bring back the dead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T18:46:23-07:00","id":1091374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090921-death-magic-for-healing-purposes?p=1091365#post1091365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't Death Unmaking straight-up bring back the dead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, minus the soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T23:27:41-07:00","id":1091439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090921-death-magic-for-healing-purposes?p=1091228#post1091228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have to consider things in a Greek perspective. Fundamentally, things exist as reflections of a platonic ideal. Each tree, for example, is a partial reflection of the fundamental supernal symbol of a tree. Trees, as all things, are not collections of molecules, bound by the laws of conservation of matter and energy, but are indivisible reflections of their corresponding symbols. The only way for a tree to deviate from the fundamental symbol of tree, is through the incorporation of other symbols into its pattern. When you chop a tree into wood, you are not breaking it apart. Things are indivisible. Rather, you are creating a new symbol of wood, and introducing a Death pattern to the tree itself. If you were to remove this Death pattern, the tree would spring back, fully formed, all of its branches and roots intact again, because there would be nothing stopping it from reflecting the fundamental tree symbol once again.<br /> <br /> So in other words, all decay, both active and past, is a foreign influence on other symbols. It must fall under an arcanum, because all things fall under an arcanum, and the most fitting arcanum for it is Death.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is now my go-to explanation for supernal symbols. Well said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T18:47:09-07:00","id":1091793,"title":"","content":"What I did when I made a Death-based 'healing' spell is that for the duration, the damage is effectively not on your sheet, as the danger/decay/'risk of death' is eaten away, but the change to the flesh itself isn't, so the wound remains superficially. You can make it lasting with +2 Reach, but still go around with horrible wounds that just kinda don't kill you. (Kinda took some inspiration from Vampiric Resilience, there).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T08:52:41-07:00","id":1112129,"title":"","content":"I think I found the perfect parallel for a healing through the Death Arcanum: the Bargain of a Sin-Eater. Here, we have a Geist, whose powers stem only from Death, who must rouse a body back to life, while. Here's a an excerpt from the corebook<br /> <br /> &quot;How is it that a geist, a creature of pure living death, can bring life back to its Sin-Eater host? Theanswer is bound up in the fact that the Bargain doesn\u2019t heal the Sin-Eater\u2019s wounds. Geists cannot actually restore life or heal a living mortal, but as archetypal figures of death, they do have an ability to manipulate death itself. In essence, the Bargain, and the attendant merging of the human soul with the inhuman geist allows the shade not to give life, but <i>to take away death</i>. This concept seems baffling, especially to humans who are accustomed to thinking of death as the absence of life, but Sin-Eaters recognize that death has a powerful energy of its own. By pushing that energy away from its new host, the geist staves off death long enough for the living body to repair itself \u2014 whether that be fighting off the disease that ravages it or knitting together bones and organs shattered by gunfire&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for the exact modalities of the healing:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Bargain brings the Sin-Eater surging back to life, but it doesn\u2019t exactly heal her. Whatever injuries brought the Sin-Eater to the brink of death linger; whatever disease killed her goes into remission but doesn\u2019t vanish overnight. Many Sin-Eaters come to understand what they\u2019ve become while lying in a hospital bed, recuperating.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't really have an opinion about what was being said earlier, and I'm pretty sure this ain't useful, but I just wanted to share that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T10:35:42-07:00","id":1112198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090921-death-magic-for-healing-purposes?p=1091037#post1091037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Good contribution...</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely lacking sarcasm, I wish I could like your post twice.<br /> <br /> I think the reasonable interpretation in my opinion is not whether Death should be able to remove damage, clearly it should deal with the issue of damage removal. <i>How </i>is the trick.<br /> <br /> My sensibilities are something like this:<br /> <br /> <b>Fraying</b> being able to remove one potency per Bashing/Lethal, but it has a normal spell Duration, and not be able to affect Aggravated at all.<ul><li>+2 Reach for making Bashing removal Lasting.</li> </ul><b>Bonus:</b> This affects any type of being capable of being damaged since the injury is the target, and leaves no scars.<br /> <br /> <b>Unraveling</b> being able to remove Lethal or Bashing Lasting on a one Potency to one damage ratio, at a Lasting duration.<ul><li>+2 reach it may affect Aggravated damage at the same ratio, but has a normal spell duration and isn't Lasting.</li> <li>+3 Reach and 1 Mana, it may affect Aggravated damage at the same ratio and is Lasting</li> </ul><b>Bonus:</b> This affects any type of being capable of being damaged since the injury is the target, and leaves no scars.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> This distinguishes it from how Life heals, making it in specialized situations more advantageous, and in common situations less, which helps makes the overlap nuanced, meaningful and interesting. Also you may ask why is healing Bashing so hard? I'd answer Death Mage Armor converts damage to Bashing and being the best at healing be a Life <u>and</u> Death thing amuses me, and discourages one Arcanum-stop-shopping<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090921-death-magic-for-healing-purposes?p=1091236#post1091236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying that it has to be this way, but it would be kinda cool if Death healing was substantively different than Life healing.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-06-2017, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}